{"text": " Every completed MPSA transaction that does not immediately trigger a WhatsApp confirmation is a missed customer experience opportunity. Every order that ships without a WhatsApp update generates a support call. Transactional alerts are the highest ROI WhatsApp automation for any Kenyan business with transactions. In this lesson, how to build event-driven WhatsApp notifications that trigger automatically from MPSA callbacks, order status changes, appointment confirmations and any other business event. Includes the template approval process, opt-in compliance and the exact code pattern for triggering messages from back-end events. We cover event-driven messaging architecture, how your back-end triggers WhatsApp messages on business events, message template creation and approval. The exact format meta requires for outbound business messages. MPSA C2B callback integration, triggering a WhatsApp confirmation on every successful payment and order lifecycle notifications, placed confirmed, shipped, delivered, failed. Transactional WhatsApp alerts work on the event-driven model. A business event occurs, payment received, order shipped, appointment confirmed, arrow. Your system detects it, arrow. Your code calls the meta API with a pre-approved template, arrow. The customer receives a WhatsApp notification within two to three seconds. The key constraint is the message template. Any message you send to a customer who has not messaged you in the last 24 hours must use a pre-approved template. Templates are plain text with numbered variable placeholders like one and two. The full MPSA to WhatsApp notification flow, one, register your C2BURL with SafariCom Darajah API, two, customer pays via MPSA, three, SafariCom posts transaction details to your C2BURL, four, verify the request is genuinely from SafariCom, check IP and credentials, five, extract phone number, amount and empecercode from the payload, six, format phone number to two, five, four, XXXXXXXXXXX, Darajah s